00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:31.820
- And since the word electromagnetic
was mentioned in there,

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:33.220
I would just say that's the word we use

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.460
to describe the entire spectrum of light,

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:38.820
not only the visible light, ROY G BIV,

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:41.100
red, orange, yellow, green,
blue, indigo, violet,

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:44.560
but the infrared, ultraviolet,
X-rays, gamma rays,

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.200
microwaves, radio waves,

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.020
all of that is the
electromagnetic spectrum.

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:52.260
Only a tiny slice of it are
we sensitive to with our eyes.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:54.780
So, what's interesting is we have

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.910
this mechanism called our eyeballs

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.890
that takes that and
turns it into an image,

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.750
