but you don't remember,

00:34:17.198 --> 00:34:18.220
then how do you know you dreamed?

00:34:18.220 --> 00:34:19.603
- Well, you don't know, but we assume.

00:34:19.603 --> 00:34:22.620
- It's of your electrodes again,
they say they're dreaming.

00:34:22.620 --> 00:34:23.840
- There's an interesting
case, just a side note,

00:34:23.840 --> 00:34:25.570
there's the case of people
who don't remember things,

00:34:25.570 --> 00:34:26.660
they only have a short memory,

00:34:26.660 --> 00:34:28.420
and so they feel like
they're just waking up

00:34:28.420 --> 00:34:30.420
and being conscious for the
first time every minute,

00:34:30.420 --> 00:34:33.580
'cause they keep refreshing,
refreshing, refreshing.

00:34:33.580 --> 00:34:35.550
But, I mean, you can have
a conscious experience

00:34:35.550 --> 00:34:37.710
and not remember it, but
still you had that experience

00:34:37.710 --> 00:34:38.610
in the moment.

00:34:38.610 --> 00:34:40.150
But the point is that these dreams,

00:34:40.150 --> 00:34:41.720
a lot of it is a cleaning out.

00:34:41.720 --> 00:34:43.270
So you've taken in a lot of information,

00:34:43.270 --> 00:34:44.380
a lot of stimulation during the day,

00:34:44.380 --> 00:34:46.010
and then the brain has to
decide what's important

00:34:46.010 --> 00:34:48.300
enough to reinstantiate,
to keep and to reinforce,

00:34:48.300 --> 00:34:49.956
and to kind of throw away, get rid of it.

00:34:49.956 --> 00:34:51.660
- Reinstantiate?
- Or reinforce.

00:34:51.660 --> 00:34:52.493
- That's a word?

00:34:52.493 --> 00:34:53.450
- Yeah, I don't know, did I make it up?

00:34:53.450 --> 00:34:54.360
I might have made that up.

00:34:54.360 --> 00:34:56.647
- Reinstantiate.
- Or just instantiate?

00:34:56.647 --> 00:34:57.956
(Heather laughs)
