00:38:18.310 --> 00:38:21.277
and that they have
consciousness, so the answer is--

00:38:21.277 --> 00:38:22.230
- So instead of putting
them in the boiling water,

00:38:22.230 --> 00:38:24.091
you kill them some other way.

00:38:24.091 --> 00:38:24.950
(laughs)
- First, yeah,

00:38:24.950 --> 00:38:26.893
and then you can, more compassion.

00:38:27.830 --> 00:38:30.405
Also, octopus, I think
that's what it is as well,

00:38:30.405 --> 00:38:34.410
you can't also kill an octopus in a way,

00:38:34.410 --> 00:38:36.310
because we know that they're
very smart and very conscious.

00:38:36.310 --> 00:38:39.830
- So is there is neurological primitivity

00:38:39.830 --> 00:38:42.205
where you would say they're
not really feeling this pain

00:38:42.205 --> 00:38:43.310
in some animal out there?

00:38:43.310 --> 00:38:46.460
- Okay, so the answer is
you don't need a brain.

00:38:46.460 --> 00:38:48.565
You do need some sort of nervous system.

00:38:48.565 --> 00:38:49.987
- Of course, you can have a
nervous system without a brain.

00:38:49.987 --> 00:38:52.810
- Without a brain, and so
like a jellyfish has that

00:38:52.810 --> 00:38:56.330
in its tentacles, it kind
of has like a neural net.

00:38:56.330 --> 00:38:59.230
So if you give it some noxious stimuli

00:38:59.230 --> 00:39:01.410
or you poke its tentacle,
it will move away,

00:39:01.410 --> 00:39:03.384
it will retract, if it's feeling pain.

00:39:03.384 --> 00:39:05.673
- Therefore, it feels it.

00:39:05.673 --> 00:39:07.640
Earthworms will move away from pain.

00:39:07.640 --> 00:39:10.950
- Right, so that's how we
kind of have to measure it

00:39:10.950 --> 00:39:13.560
behaviorally, because even with a human,

00:39:13.560 --> 00:39:14.900
the pain, again, it's a subjectivity.

00:39:14.900 --> 00:39:16.550
When you go to the
hospital, something's wrong,

00:39:16.550 --> 00:39:17.940
and they say okay on a scale of one to 10,

00:39:17.940 --> 00:39:18.902
how painful is it?

00:39:18.902 --> 00:39:20.640
- No, now they have a
smiley face or a sad face.

00:39:20.640 --> 00:39:22.611
(laughs)
- Oh yeah, that's right, yeah.

00:39:22.611 --> 00:39:23.444
- And numbers, the numbers.

00:39:23.444 --> 00:39:24.310
- 'Cause people, they
couldn't handle the numbers.

00:39:24.310 --> 00:39:25.143
- Nope, the numbers, let's just do--

00:39:25.143 --> 00:39:28.343
- It's too much, too much, gotta simplify.

00:39:29.680 --> 00:39:31.990
So we don't know, but
we can tell okay, look,

00:39:31.990 --> 00:39:33.560
you retract as if you're feeling pain.

00:39:33.560 --> 00:39:35.440
I was at a home meeting
where we were talking about

00:39:35.440 --> 00:39:38.880
animal consciousness and
how low down the food chain

00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:42.440
does it go, and we had a
whole discussion about fish.

00:39:42.440 --> 00:39:44.070
And fish, can they feel?

00:39:44.070 --> 00:39:46.120
And the answer is yes.

00:39:46.120 --> 00:39:48.470
Again, they have a noxious
stimuli, they'll retract from it.

00:39:48.470 --> 00:39:51.400
They record a memory so they'll
avoid that stimuli again.

00:39:51.400 --> 00:39:53.400
So it's as if they're
experiencing something.

00:39:53.400 --> 00:39:55.840
- So how do they kill the lobster

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:57.270
before you cook it?

00:39:57.270 --> 00:39:58.888
- I don't know.
- Lethal injection.

00:39:58.888 --> 00:40:00.450
- Lethal injection.
(Heather laughs)

00:40:00.450 --> 00:40:02.730
By the way, by the way,
we had on Star Talk,

00:40:02.730 --> 00:40:05.230
I interviewed the founder of PETA.

00:40:05.230 --> 00:40:06.063
- [Heather] Oh.

00:40:06.063 --> 00:40:09.210
- And many people associate
PETA with just being

00:40:10.620 --> 00:40:13.220
all veggie, no killing of animals.

00:40:13.220 --> 00:40:16.680
To hear her speak, the
philosophy was very different.

00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:19.160
It was not that she's
against killing animals,

00:40:19.160 --> 00:40:22.785
she's against the infliction
of pain on animals.

00:40:22.785 --> 00:40:23.620
- [Heather] Mm-hm.

00:40:23.620 --> 00:40:25.950
- And I said, well what about lobster?

00:40:25.950 --> 00:40:28.680
She said she has people working on

00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:33.190
some kind of anesthetizing
first pass at the lobster

00:40:33.190 --> 00:40:35.330
before you then put it
in the boiling water.

00:40:35.330 --> 00:40:36.449
- Yeah.

00:40:36.449 --> 00:40:38.513
- Just to show you the purity
of that mission statement.

00:40:39.467 --> 00:40:41.970
So I bet you if there was package of that

00:40:41.970 --> 00:40:44.070
sold next to the lobsters
people would buy it, of course.

00:40:44.070 --> 00:40:45.040
- Yeah.

00:40:45.040 --> 00:40:47.580
- Of course, I think people would do that.

00:40:47.580 --> 00:40:49.050
If you're rich enough to buy the lobster,

00:40:49.050 --> 00:40:51.556
you've got enough money to
buy the lobster anesthetizer.

00:40:51.556 --> 00:40:52.657
- Yes.
- Before you cook it.

00:40:52.657 --> 00:40:54.140
- And just, wait, minor correction,

00:40:54.140 --> 00:40:57.730
I think it's the illegality in the EU is

00:40:57.730 --> 00:41:00.458
for octopus, or octopi, I never know.

00:41:00.458 --> 00:41:01.436
- [Neil] Octopoid.

00:41:01.436 --> 00:41:02.570
- Octopoid.
- Yes.

00:41:02.570 --> 00:41:04.880
- Not lobsters, I just remembered that

00:41:04.880 --> 00:41:06.400
in the recesses of my mind.

00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:08.810
So you can still horribly damage a lobster

00:41:08.810 --> 00:41:09.700
when you boil it alive.

00:41:09.700 --> 00:41:12.850
However, I think that the real issues is

00:41:12.850 --> 00:41:15.290
about how animals are treated,

00:41:15.290 --> 00:41:17.790
and if they are killed in a
way that doesn't cause them

00:41:17.790 --> 00:41:19.967
drama, or trauma or stress.

00:41:19.967 --> 00:41:21.360
- Drama. (laughs)
- Drama.

00:41:21.360 --> 00:41:22.560
We don't want drama, either.
(laughs)

00:41:22.560 --> 00:41:23.550
- The drama queen.

00:41:23.550 --> 00:41:24.820
- I do.
- Exactly.

00:41:24.820 --> 00:41:25.880
Or you know, like Temple Grandin.

00:41:25.880 --> 00:41:27.317
- We have an actor here who wants drama.

00:41:27.317 --> 00:41:29.326
(Heather laughs)

00:41:29.326 --> 00:41:31.130
Oh, can I tell you my
drama, my bit of drama?

00:41:31.130 --> 00:41:31.963
- Mm-hm.

00:41:31.963 --> 00:41:33.920
- I know it's lame, but I still do it.

00:41:33.920 --> 00:41:35.890
Any time I cook a lobster,

00:41:35.890 --> 00:41:37.690
before I put it in the water

00:41:37.690 --> 00:41:39.860
I remove the rubber bands from the claws.

00:41:39.860 --> 00:41:42.140
- [Heather] Aw, you free it?

00:41:42.140 --> 00:41:45.740
- So that it can try to bite me

00:41:46.820 --> 00:41:48.803
as its one last act of survival.

00:41:48.803 --> 00:41:51.472
- That is like, really sadistic, I think.

00:41:51.472 --> 00:41:52.643
(Heather and Neil laugh)

00:41:52.643 --> 00:41:54.493
- You went deep into that lobster mind.

00:41:54.493 --> 00:41:55.326
- I'm saying, if I'm cooking it alive,

00:41:55.326 --> 00:41:57.733
at least give it a chance to fight back.

00:41:57.733 --> 00:41:58.566
- Aw.

00:41:58.566 --> 00:42:01.110
- So I take off the rubber
bands and then they pop open,

00:42:01.110 --> 00:42:02.360
the claws pop open.
- Oh, God.

00:42:02.360 --> 00:42:04.820
- And then it can try to bite me,

00:42:04.820 --> 00:42:07.790
and I have to then triumph over it.

00:42:07.790 --> 00:42:09.707
Of course I do.
- Wow, wow.

00:42:09.707 --> 00:42:10.624
- 'Cause I'm smarter than a lobster.

00:42:10.624 --> 00:42:12.176
- So you give him one fighting chance?

00:42:12.176 --> 00:42:14.020
(Heather laughs)
- One last chance,

00:42:14.020 --> 00:42:15.790
It's my own--
- So he can die with dignity?

00:42:15.790 --> 00:42:18.160
- Dignity, thank you,
thank you, thank you.

00:42:18.160 --> 00:42:19.292
- Oh my God.

00:42:19.292 --> 00:42:20.747
- Okay, so tell me about Temple Grandin.

00:42:20.747 --> 00:42:21.580
- I was just gonna say, Temple Grandin.

00:42:21.580 --> 00:42:23.320
- Who, by the way, has
been a guest on Star Talk.

00:42:23.320 --> 00:42:25.771
- Oh, she's great.
- One of my favorite shows.

00:42:25.771 --> 00:42:27.029
- Oh, so interesting.
- Temple Grandin.

00:42:27.029 --> 00:42:30.280
- So she has autism, and
she was very much aware of,

00:42:30.280 --> 00:42:32.860
she can sort of empathize with
how the animals were feeling,

00:42:32.860 --> 00:42:34.580
and she created this whole system of

00:42:34.580 --> 00:42:38.890
when they go to slaughter,
that they would gently be,

00:42:38.890 --> 00:42:41.830
so it wasn't stressful for
them or anxiety-provoking.

00:42:41.830 --> 00:42:44.760
They would get guided
through this sort of,

00:42:44.760 --> 00:42:47.170
they were kind of like tunnels
into the slaughterhouse

00:42:47.170 --> 00:42:48.550
in a way that was so they couldn't see

00:42:48.550 --> 00:42:50.050
what was happening in front of them.

00:42:50.050 --> 00:42:52.020
And it was like this really humane way

00:42:52.020 --> 00:42:54.570
to bring them there without
just throwing them in

00:42:54.570 --> 00:42:55.741
and giving them all the anxiety of stress

00:42:55.741 --> 00:42:56.574
like they're about to die.

00:42:56.574 --> 00:42:57.870
- Corralling them, and then in there.

00:42:57.870 --> 00:42:59.840
- Yeah, and so I thought
that was really humane.

00:42:59.840 --> 00:43:01.460
- Plus, there are people
in the vegetarian movement

00:43:01.460 --> 00:43:04.043
that hate her for that,
because she made it

00:43:04.043 --> 00:43:06.430
that much more humane to kill an animal

00:43:06.430 --> 00:43:08.690
that the vegetarians didn't
want killed in the first place.

00:43:08.690 --> 00:43:11.000
- Yes, yes, so we can go deeper into that.

00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:12.700
But the answer is you don't need a brain,

00:43:12.700 --> 00:43:14.300
but you need, I think, a nervous system.

00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:15.510
- Okay, cool.

00:43:15.510 --> 00:43:17.730
All right, we've got to go
lightning round, Jackie.

00:43:17.730 --> 00:43:19.713
- Lightning.
- Let me try to.

00:43:20.559 --> 00:43:21.392
(bell dings)

00:43:21.392 --> 00:43:22.381
- Oh, this is scary.
- There we go.

00:43:22.381 --> 00:43:23.450
