on your sound bites.

00:43:25.240 --> 00:43:26.870
Okay, here we go, Jackie, give it to me.

00:43:26.870 --> 00:43:28.890
- From San Pangoso on Facebook,

00:43:28.890 --> 00:43:31.220
how are memories physically
stored in the brain?

00:43:31.220 --> 00:43:35.150
Also, can we implant fabricated
memories in some way?

00:43:35.150 --> 00:43:36.200
- [Neil] Ooh.
- Yes.

00:43:38.357 --> 00:43:41.780
(laughs)
In the brain via long term

00:43:41.780 --> 00:43:43.990
potentiation, which is a physical process

00:43:43.990 --> 00:43:45.720
that connects neurons to each other,

00:43:45.720 --> 00:43:49.420
or makes them what fires
together wires together,

00:43:49.420 --> 00:43:51.920
that's the quickest, Hebbian
synapse, it's called.

00:43:51.920 --> 00:43:53.380
- Cool, so the more they fire together

00:43:53.380 --> 00:43:55.003
the more they will remain connected?

00:43:55.003 --> 00:43:55.880
- Yes, yes.

00:43:55.880 --> 00:43:57.540
- In such a way that they form a memory?

00:43:57.540 --> 00:43:58.840
- Yes.
- Next one, quick.

00:43:59.760 --> 00:44:01.490
- I've Always Been Your
Sancho on Instagram,

00:44:01.490 --> 00:44:03.320
what does it mean to focus on something,

00:44:03.320 --> 00:44:04.153
how does it work?

00:44:04.153 --> 00:44:05.133
- Ooh, good one, attention span.

00:44:05.133 --> 00:44:07.130
- That means attention, it's attention,

00:44:07.130 --> 00:44:08.680
and what it is, is
there's part of your brain

00:44:08.680 --> 00:44:10.834
called the dorsolateral prefrontal
cortex that's activated.

00:44:10.834 --> 00:44:12.346
- That's way too many syllables,
you all gotta work on that.

00:44:12.346 --> 00:44:15.167
- The DFLPC.
(Neil laughs)

00:44:15.167 --> 00:44:18.620
- No, DLFPC, anyway, so you can engage

00:44:18.620 --> 00:44:20.290
certain parts of your prefrontal cortex

00:44:20.290 --> 00:44:22.840
that filter out extraneous information,

00:44:22.840 --> 00:44:26.130
and your mental energy is focused on

00:44:26.130 --> 00:44:27.498
a particular bit of information.

00:44:27.498 --> 00:44:29.410
- So part of the focus
is taking away things

00:44:29.410 --> 00:44:30.270
that would distract.

00:44:30.270 --> 00:44:31.750
- Yes, yes, and that's why people who have

00:44:31.750 --> 00:44:32.810
problems with their attention is

00:44:32.810 --> 00:44:34.050
that they're too easily distracted,

00:44:34.050 --> 00:44:37.041
they're not good at focusing
in because of the distractions.

00:44:37.041 --> 00:44:37.874
- Cool.
(bell dings)

00:44:37.874 --> 00:44:38.707
Got it.
- What?

